      "blockKey": "evidence",
      "text": "He did not stop arguing when he turned. He kept trying to look back while moving a frightened survivor ahead of him. The movement was awkward, divided between two duties. It was neither the obedience of a follower nor the clean decision his later guilt insisted it must have been.",
      "mode": "SILENT_HANDWRITING",
      "textSHA256": "8404c5f3e3c3dad8eff86a2e8ba86e731d09d4e91431cc2306ef3c8e754bc443"
    },
    {
      "blockKey": "account",
      "text": "This does not make the loss just. It does not prove that another choice would have saved everyone. It restores the people his account had cropped away. While one friend remained beyond his reach, others were within it. He could fail to keep them together and still have acted for more than himself.",
      "mode": "SILENT_HANDWRITING",
