  "journalText": "The warrior's last backward glance had become the whole of this memory. Beyond its edge, others were still trying to leave. One had lost a shoe. Another could not lift the arm that held a borrowed cloak. The warrior reached them while the voice behind the barrier was still calling.\n\nHe left because his friend's command mattered more than his own conviction.\n\nHe left to lead the others out, without consenting to the separation he could not prevent.\n\nHe did not stop arguing when he turned. He kept trying to look back while moving a frightened survivor ahead of him. The movement was awkward, divided between two duties. It was neither the obedience of a follower nor the clean decision his later guilt insisted it must have been.\n\nThis does not make the loss just. It does not prove that another choice would have saved everyone. It restores the people his account had cropped away. While one friend remained beyond his reach, others were within it. He could fail to keep them together and still have acted for more than himself.\n\nThe separation was real. So were the lives he could still reach when he turned away.",
  "wordCount": 197,
  "newlyRecoveredInformation": "His departure included immediate responsibility for vulnerable survivors, and did not express agreement with erasure or abandonment.",
  "newlyAuthoredDetails": [
    "Unnamed evacuees at the edge of the barrier memory; the original command and resistance remain intact."
  ],
